{"name":"Pharlap","hex":"#826663","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Phar Lap","blocks":[{"text":"Phar Lap was a New Zealand–born champion Australian Thoroughbred racehorse. Achieving great success during his distinguished career, his initial underdog status gave people hope during the early years of the Great Depression. He won the Melbourne Cup, two Cox Plates, the Australian Derby, and 19 other weight-for-age races. He is considered one of the greatest race horses of all time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Phar_Lap.jpg/330px-Phar_Lap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phar_Lap","wikidata":"Q379362"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Phar_Lap_competing_in_a_race%2C_Melbourne%2C_ca._1930_.jpg/500px-Phar_Lap_competing_in_a_race%2C_Melbourne%2C_ca._1930_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Phar_Lap_competing_in_a_race%2C_Melbourne%2C_ca._1930_.jpg/500px-Phar_Lap_competing_in_a_race%2C_Melbourne%2C_ca._1930_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Phar Lap Jim Pike and Chide W.Cook Randwick Racecourse 1931","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhar_Lap_competing_in_a_race%2C_Melbourne%2C_ca._1930_.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Pharlap1930melbournecup.jpg/500px-Pharlap1930melbournecup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Pharlap1930melbournecup.jpg/500px-Pharlap1930melbournecup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Phar Lap winning the Melbourne Cup Race from Second Wind and Shadow King on 4 November 1930","link":"https://en.wikipedia.